The '''Savarians''' were a cultural group of [[human]]s who called the the [[Outer Rim Territories]] [[planet]] [[Savareen]] [[Homeworld|home]]. They were a deeply spiritual people and lived in scattered villages, including the [[Pnakotic Coast village]] with it's [[Bis Refinery]].<ref name="TOG" /> 

After [[Uprising on Savareen|a failed uprising]] against a group of plundering [[Mercenary|mercenaries]] which later became the crime syndicate [[Crimson Dawn]], all the Savarians villagers had their [[tongue]]s cut out as retribution,<ref name="Solo">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> which forced them to speak in a [[sign language]].<ref name="TOG" /> One of the people in the uprising was [[Unidentified Savarian priest|a priest]], who was later venerated as a martyr.<ref name="Sanctuary">''[[Sanctuary: A Bad Batch Novel]]''</ref> Other Savarians included [[Krysguld Dartis]], [[Kenholdt Ransard]], [[Taraja Cuttsmay]], [[Yirpa Garajon]], [[Dhowar Repareed]], [[Vamasto Maja]], and [[Lanzarota Malco]]. The Savarians believed that dead returned to the beaches after dying. They memorialized their late loved ones in spires placed next to the ocean, which they called "[[soultheeth]]" and believed that they acted as an anchor for their spirits.<ref name="TOG" />

